    "format-version": "0.1",
    "license": "MIT",
    "name": "IPK2026_Metagenomics_ARG_Pipeline",
    "readme": "# IPK2026 Metagenomics — BGC & Drug Target Discovery Pipeline\n\nMetagenomics pipeline for taxonomic profiling, known ARG detection, and novel drug target discovery via biosynthetic gene cluster (BGC) mining.\n\n## Dataset\nPRJNA781406 (Vanishing Glaciers Project — glacier-fed stream biofilms; Busi/Kohler/Battin et al. 2023, Microbiology Spectrum, PMC9927545)\n- Default sample: SRR14689470 (GL_R17_GL16_UP_1), one of 21 confirmed samples from 8 glacier sites (GL5, GL11, GL15, GL16 New Zealand; GL46, GL47, GL53, GL56 Russian Caucasus)\n- Illumina NovaSeq 6000, 151bp paired-end, ~96.5M reads (smallest of the 21 confirmed samples)\n- Original paper confirms BOTH known-ARG signal (1,840 ARGs via CARD-based PathoFact/RGI/DeepARG) AND BGC signal (91% of 490 MAGs via antiSMASH+deepBGC+GECCO) in this same dataset\n- Switched 2026-07-12 from the original PRJNA717813 (Schönbuch Forest soil, mSystems 2021), which produced 0 ABRicate/CARD hits at 80-90% identity even from a 1.4Gbp assembly (see WORKFLOW_VERIFICATION.md section 7.10-7.11 for the diagnostic trail and dataset-selection reasoning)\n\n## Input\nProvide Illumina NovaSeq paired-end FASTQ collection from PRJNA781406.\nRun fasterq-dump with SRR accessions first, then select 'Paired-end data' collection.\nPfam-A.hmm database file required for BiG-SCAPE (step 16).\n\n## Pipeline\n\n### Taxa Profiling\nfastp → Kraken2 (PlusPF) → Bracken → kreport2krona → Krona (multi-sample)\n- Alpha diversity (Shannon H')\n- Beta diversity (Bray-Curtis)\n\n### Known ARG Pool (→ IPK2026 #16 Transcriptomics)\n- Branch A: fastp reads (forward only) → GROOT (arg-annot) → CARD family normalize\n- Branch B: MEGAHIT contigs → ABRicate/CARD → ABRicate Summary\n- Branch A vs B comparison: method-sensitivity check (reads-only / contigs-only ARGs)\n\n### Novel Drug Target Discovery (→ IPK2026 #17 Cheminformatics, #18 AI)\n1. MEGAHIT → antiSMASH (BGC prediction + MIBiG comparison + RRE)\n2. BiG-SCAPE (BGC novelty — Gene Cluster Family clustering with --mibig)\n3. Branch C: antiSMASH GenBank → ABRicate/CARD (BGC-encoded ARGs)\n4. ABRicate Summary → zero-hit guard → Transpose → ARG Name Normalization (awk, CARD ARO Gene Family):\n   - TEM-1, TEM-15 → TEM beta-lactamase (same family → join matches correctly)\n5. Join unmatched: BGC ARGs NOT in assembly ARG pool = BGC-exclusive ARGs\n   = Self-resistance gene candidates = NOVEL DRUG TARGETS\n\n## ARG Name Standardization\nBoth ABRicate runs use the same CARD database version, ensuring name consistency.\nThe normalization step (awk) maps every gene name to its CARD ARO AMR Gene Family (built from CARD's own aro_index.tsv), so allele-level variants join correctly.\n\n## IPK2026 Lecture Connections\n- #14 Hit-to-Lead: Predicted drug targets → HTS design\n- #15 Natural Products: BGC → compound structure prediction\n- #16 Transcriptomics: Known ARGs → resistance mechanism understanding\n- #17 Cheminformatics: Drug target → molecular docking → virtual screening\n- #18 AI for Drug Discovery: Drug target → AI-based binding prediction\n\n## Platform\nusegalaxy.eu",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "# IPK2026 Metagenomics ARG Pipeline Results\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n\n## Taxa Profiling (Krona)\n```galaxy\nhistory_dataset_display(output=\"krona_chart\")\n```\n\n## ARG Detection — Branch A (reads-based)\n```galaxy\nhistory_dataset_display(output=\"abricate_reads_summary\")\n```\n\n## ARG Detection — Branch B (assembly-based)\n```galaxy\nhistory_dataset_display(output=\"abricate_contigs_summary\")\n```\n\n## ARG Detection — Branch C (BGC sequences)\n```galaxy\nhistory_dataset_display(output=\"abricate_bgc_summary\")\n```\n\n## Novel Drug Targets (BGC-exclusive ARGs)\n```galaxy\nhistory_dataset_display(output=\"novel_drug_targets\")\n```\n"
    },
    "steps": {
        "0": {
            "annotation": "SRR/DRR/ERR accession number. Default: SRR14689470 (GL_R17_GL16_UP_1, glacier-fed stream biofilm, PRJNA781406, Busi/Kohler/Battin et al. 2023 Microbiology Spectrum PMC9927545). Chosen 2026-07-12 to replace the original PRJNA717813 forest soil sample, which showed 0 ABRicate/CARD hits at 80-90% identity in the assembled contigs even from a 1.4Gbp assembly — the original paper for THIS dataset confirms both resistome (1,840 ARGs via CARD-based PathoFact/RGI/DeepARG) and BGC (91% of MAGs via antiSMASH+deepBGC+GECCO) signal are present. Verified directly against the paper's own supplementary Table S5 (BioSample accessions) that this exact run is among the 21 samples/8 sites actually analyzed in that paper (not just anywhere in the broader 2,240-run BioProject). Reads are 151bp (confirmed by downloading and inspecting the raw FASTQ directly) — functionally identical to the previous 150bp assumption, so GROOT windowSize/Bracken kmer_distr choices made earlier still apply unchanged. Read depth ~96.5M reads (paired), smallest of the paper's 21 samples, chosen to keep assembly runtime manageable for a live demo.",
