        "4": {
            "annotation": "Bayesian re-estimation of species-level abundances from Kraken2 report. read_length: 150bp, level: S (species), threshold: 10 reads. [2026-07-10 fix: kmer_distr corrected to match Kraken2's actual database (PlusPF, Version 2022-06-07) — was pointing to an unrelated PlusPF-8/2024-01-12 entry, which would have made Bracken's abundance re-estimation scientifically invalid even though it would not have crashed. Stale 'database'/'length' keys removed (not real params in bracken 3.1+galaxy0, only kmer_distr is). Read:100 is the closest available option; no PlusPF/150 build exists on usegalaxy.eu as of this check.] [2026-07-10 caveat: kmer_distr uses the 100bp PlusPF/2022-06-07 build (matching Kraken2's DB) because no 150bp PlusPF option exists on usegalaxy.eu. Bracken's own manual documents building per-read-length distributions but does not address substituting the nearest available length — this is a pragmatic approximation, not an officially validated equivalence. Present as such, not as fully correct.]",
