        "15": {
            "annotation": "Clusters BGCs into Gene Cluster Families (GCFs) based on domain-content similarity among the sample's own antiSMASH-detected BGCs. inputs: inputdir (antiSMASH genbank collection) + pfam_dir (Pfam-A.hmm, hmm3 format). cutoff repeat --cutoffs=0.3. [2026-07-18 fix: --mibig disabled. BiG-SCAPE 1.1.9's container has a deterministic bug — it tries to lazily unzip its bundled MIBiG reference into its own read-only site-packages directory on every run, confirmed via source (bigscape.py v1.1.9 lines 2305-2349, no CLI/env override exists) and a matching unresolved Galaxy help-forum report. No newer Galaxy wrapper or alternative (e.g. BiG-SLICE) is available on usegalaxy.eu. This is NOT a functional loss for the 'known vs novel compound' question though: antiSMASH (Step 14) already runs its own MIBiG comparison per-BGC via cb_knownclusters/cc_mibig, independent of BiG-SCAPE and unaffected by this bug. BiG-SCAPE's remaining (and genuinely unique) contribution is cross-BGC family clustering + network visualization among this sample's own BGCs, which doesn't need MIBiG.] Use html+tsv output + antiSMASH genbank with ARTS (arts.ziemertlab.com) to find self-resistance genes → Novel Drug Targets (→ IPK2026 #17 Cheminformatics).",
            "content_id": "toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/iuc/bigscape/bigscape/1.1.9+galaxy2",
