        },
        "28": {
            "annotation": "ARG-ANNOT→CARD Family Normalize — Branch A. Maps GROOT/ARG-ANNOT reference gene IDs to the same CARD AMR Gene Family vocabulary used by Branch B/C, so Branch A is directly comparable (method-sensitivity check: reads vs contigs). Mapping built by chaining two public reference tables (no argnorm tool run needed, same technique as the CARD ARO normalize steps): (1) argNorm's groot_ARO_mapping.tsv (github.com/BigDataBiology/argNorm) maps GROOT arg-annot reference IDs → ARO accession, using argNorm's own published matching key (accession:start-end, extracted from the reference ID); (2) CARD's aro_index.tsv maps ARO accession → AMR Gene Family. Chained and hardcoded into this awk map (1,804 entries, see groot_gene_family_map.tsv). Fallback: toupper() for any GROOT hit not in the mapping.",
            "content_id": "toolshed.g2.bx.psu.edu/repos/bgruening/text_processing/tp_awk_tool/1.1.2",
            "errors": null,
            "id": 28,
            "input_connections": {
                "infile": {
                    "id": 27,
                    "output_name": "report_out"
                }
            },
            "inputs": [],
            "label": "CARD Family Normalize — Branch A (GROOT)",
            "name": "Text reformatting with awk",
            "outputs": [
